<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87413" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προερέω</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		
			contr.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προερῶ</span></b> , serving as
		fut. to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προεῖπον</span>(q.v.): also
			pf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προείρηκα,</span>
		
			Pass.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ημαι</span>: aor.
		
			Pass.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προερρήθην,</span>
		
			contr.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προὐρρήθην</span>:— <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>say beforehand,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				292d
			</span></i>, etc.:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ τῶν προειρημένων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Phd.</u>
					75b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ τὰ π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>R.</u>
					408c
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς π. συμφωνεῖν</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				398c
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ προρρηθέντα</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				619c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῦτά μοι προειρήσθω</span>”
				<i>be said by way of preface,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					4.14
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				5.29
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>order beforehand</i> or <i>publicly,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συλλέγεσθαι ἐς Σάρδις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.77
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				81
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τῷ στρατῷ ὡς . . ἀκουστέα εἴη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					3.61
				</span></i>
			:— 
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προὐρρήθη ὅπως . .</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					198e
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προείρητο αὐτοῖς μὴ ἐπιχειρεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					2.84
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				6.40
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔχοντες τὸ προειρημένον</span>
			the <i>prescribed</i> implement, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.126
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπικέσθαι ἐς τὴν π. ἡμέρην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					6.128
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεῖπνον . . ἐκ πολλοῦ χρόνου π.</span>”
				<i>ordered beforehand,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					7.119
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλεμος προερρήθη</span>”
				<i>was declared,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Ages.</u>
					1.17
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀνυμαστὶ προερεῖ</span>
			<i>will call</i> him <i>publicly</i> by name, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Berl.Sitzb.</u>
				1927.167
			</span></i>(<span class="entity">Cyrene</span>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
